================================================================================
WHAT THIS MEANS, IN SHORT
================================================================================

This summary is not the licence. The licence text decides. The summary helps
you to read the licence.

You MAY:

  - Read this material.
  - Copy it and give it to other people, without change.
  - Use it inside your organisation, to learn from it.

You MAY NOT:

  - Use it for commercial purposes. You may not sell it, and you may not teach
    it for payment.
  - Publish a changed version of it.

You MUST:

  - Give credit to the author.
  - Give a link to the licence.
  - Say whether you changed anything. (You may not publish a changed version,
    but you must still be honest about changes that you make for yourself.)

================================================================================
NOTE ON THE SKILLS
================================================================================

The method that this workshop teaches lives in the `skills/` directory. Those
files are MIT licensed. You may use them, change them, and build on them, also
for commercial work. If you want to apply the method to your own code base,
then use the skills. That is what they are for.

The restriction here protects the teaching material only: the talk, the
notebooks, and the order in which the subject is presented.

